# CODEOWNERS — Quiver is a single-maintainer repository today; the
# `@crochee` placeholder is replaced at the GitHub-org level when the
# project gains co-maintainers or a sponsoring organisation. Until then
# every file defaults to the repo owner.
#
# Patterns are last-match-wins; section comments group by domain.
# Reference: <https://docs.github.com/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners>

# Default for everything not matched below.
/                                       @crochee

# CI / supply-chain attestation is the highest-risk surface; require an
# extra pair of eyes even from the owner before any change ships.
/.github/                                @crochee
/Dockerfile                              @crochee
/build.rs                                @crochee

# Release process is policy-bearing; the same gate.
/RELEASE.md                              @crochee